  "h_rev_implication": {
    "what_losing_to_markov_means": "H-rev asks whether a probe's ranking vs baselines reverses when the action unit changes (native vs matched clusters). Markov order-1 is the parameter-light 1-step successor table. If GRU loses to Markov at a unit, that unit's GRU 'win' vs popularity/recency is not a learned-structure win: a count table already captures the regularity (sticky or curriculum-order). A confirmatory H-rev claim at that unit cannot treat GRU as beating the required baseline set. Native XES (7,439 questions, mode successor \u22480.35, GRU 0.614 vs Markov 0.739 at freeze) is therefore descriptive. The informative contrast is the cluster unit, where GRU can still beat Markov.",
